okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: `meta model api를 사용해서, muse 를 실행할때는. api key를 주입을 안해? 라우터 모드가 동작을안해?` - verify (a) whether a Muse launch injects the configured Meta Model API key and (b) whether `ciel-runtime muse --ca-router` works on this machine. Question only; no fix was requested."
answer:
  api_key_native: "True - and by design. Native `ciel-runtime muse` removes META_API_KEY and MODEL_API_KEY from the child environment (muse_runtime_context.py:21-22, 622-625) and the WSL prefix runs `env -u META_API_KEY -u MODEL_API_KEY` (muse_runtime_context.py:325-339). The Meta key stored in the ciel-runtime config is never handed to Muse; Muse is meant to use its own login (docs/Muse-Code.md 'Authentication and billing boundary'; unit tests test_native_launch_preserves_browser_subscription_and_uses_channel_proxy, test_windows_launch_uses_wsl_and_unsets_linux_api_key_environment)."
  api_key_routed: "The launcher does set the router token into the child env in routed mode (muse_runtime_context.py:626-630), but on Windows it cannot reach the Muse process: Windows environment variables do not enter WSL (measured - a Windows META_API_KEY is invisible to `wsl -e sh -lc` with AND without the launcher's `env -u` prefix), and the prefix strips those names anyway. Live: the muse process sent its own stored credential (User-Agent muse-build/1.3.0, Authorization 'Bearer LLM|...' from ~/.config/muse/auth.json), not the launcher token."
  router_mode: "It does not work on this machine with Muse 1.3.0-R3401.1, verified live. (1) Router on loopback -> the launcher refuses (exit 2) because Muse runs in WSL. (2) With `--ca-web-address 172.29.112.1` the launch proceeds and the router really runs (bound to the WSL-reachable address, external token ensured, clean stop on exit) - but Muse withholds the Meta bearer for any base_url that is 'off the sanctioned front door', so the model call cannot authenticate: exit 1 with `Meta bearer withheld: base_url is off the sanctioned front door...` / `meta provider resolution did not construct its credential-provider handle`. Muse's own opt-in text names settings `endpoint_transport` + pinned `auth = \"bearer\"` and states a settings pin does not vouch for a `--base-url` flag - which is exactly how the launcher passes the router URL."
evidence:
  live_launch_without_web_address: "From a scratch workspace (C:\\Users\\djlov\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\muse-router-probe-20260921, CIEL_RUNTIME_* scrubbed) with the deployed CLI: `muse --ca-router exec ping` -> exit 2, 'Muse Code runs inside WSL and cannot reach the Ciel Router at http://127.0.0.1:9494. ... --ca-web-address <windows-wsl-ip>'."
  live_launch_with_web_address: "Same CLI with `--ca-web-address 172.29.112.1`: router instance 9494-47bd9338be61 started on 172.29.112.1:9494 (router.log: 'ciel-runtime router starting on 172.29.112.1:9494', router_spawned running=True, then router_kill_guarantee reason=claude_exit / router_lifetime_stopped), Muse exec exited 1 with the sanctioned-front-door message; no request ever reached the router."
  muse_policy_text_in_binary: "`grep -a` on /home/djlov/.local/bin/muse-bin-1.3.0-R3401.1 (313,800,920 bytes, mtime 2026-09-19 01:35) finds the message once, next to its settings schema (`settings.endpoint_transport`, `settings.endpoint_transport.base_url`, `endpoint_transport.resolve`, `bearer`, `missing_api_key`). It is Muse's own policy, not ciel-runtime's."
  capture_loopback: "Control A - `muse exec --provider meta --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8791/v1` (no META_API_KEY, launcher-style `env -u`): Muse DID send the request to the loopback listener - GET /muse-code/models and POST /v1/responses with `Authorization: Bearer LLM|1599669758238987|KUoi...` (its stored credential) and x-client-id tbh:exec; the run then failed only on the listener's 401. So loopback endpoints are 'vouched'; this is the shape the 2026-09-18 capture saw."
  capture_nonloopback: "Control B - same exec against the Windows host, `--base-url http://172.29.112.1:8792/v1` (the exact routed topology), with META_API_KEY=dummy-key-123 set: the withheld warning printed, and every request (GET /muse-code/models, POST /v1/responses from 172.29.114.158) arrived with `authorization: null` - neither the stored credential nor the env key is attached; the run ended `API error 401: capture listener`."
  wsl_env: "Windows META_API_KEY=PROBE-VALUE-123 -> `wsl -e sh -lc 'echo ${META_API_KEY}'` prints <absent>, and the launcher-style `wsl -e env -u META_API_KEY -u MODEL_API_KEY ...` also prints <absent>. Windows env vars are not shared into WSL, so the routed token injection cannot work from the Windows side."
  wsl_to_windows_path: "Pure connectivity from WSL to the Windows host address works: the requests in control B reached 172.29.112.1:8792 from 172.29.114.158. The failure is the credential policy plus the router's own external-token requirement, not the network."
  router_auth: "Code (ciel_runtime_support/router_access.py request_allowed): a non-loopback client is allowed only when external access is enabled AND the request carries the router's external-access token. Muse sends no Authorization for the router URL at all, so even without the Muse policy the router would answer 401."
  config_state: "The Meta Model API key IS now configured (providers.meta.api_key, base_url https://api.meta.ai/v1) - the 2026-09-18 prerequisite 'no key anywhere on this machine' no longer holds; the key stays in the router/config and is still not handed to Muse."
  muse_version: "Muse Code 1.3.0 (1.3.0-R3401.1); the routed design was captured against R3233.1 on 2026-09-18, i.e. a different build."
confirmed_vs_inferred:
  confirmed: "Native launches strip the key (code+tests); the routed token never reaches Muse on Windows (measured); `--ca-router` fails on this machine in both the no-flag and --ca-web-address forms (live runs above); loopback base URLs receive Muse's stored credential while the non-loopback router address does not (both captured)."
  inferred: "That the same withholding applies to every non-loopback host on this build (tested on the Windows WSL host address only); that R3233.1 lacked the rule (its capture used a loopback listener, so it cannot show the difference)."
  not_tested: "No live Muse->router call with a vouchable endpoint, because the launcher has no way to write Muse's settings `endpoint_transport` today; no change was made anywhere."
leftovers:
  - "Router instance dir router-instances/9494-47bd9338be61 (log + external token) and a workspace-router-ports.json entry for the temp workspace - left as evidence; the router itself stopped cleanly."
  - "Probe scripts and capture logs: %TEMP%\\muse-router-probe-20260921 (capture.py, capture_win.py, win-capture.log from the Windows listener, wsl-capture.log from the WSL listener)."
  - "Two headless exec sessions exist under WSL ~/.local/share/muse/sessions (workspace /home/djlov/muse-router-probe) - the workspace directory itself was removed, the session records were left alone."
not_done: "No code or docs change: the request was a question. docs/Muse-Code.md still describes routed mode as the pay-as-you-go path; the live result above contradicts it for Muse 1.3.0-R3401.1."
sources:
  - "ciel_runtime_support/muse_runtime_context.py (env handling 622-630, WSL prefix 325-339), ciel_runtime_support/runtime_adapters.py (MuseRuntimeAdapter), ciel_runtime_support/router_access.py (request_allowed, bind_host), ciel_runtime_support/web_endpoints.py (_apply_web_host), ciel_runtime_support/runtime_paths.py (ROUTER_BASE), docs/Muse-Code.md."
  - "/home/djlov/.local/bin/muse-bin-1.3.0-R3401.1 - policy message and endpoint_transport schema strings."
  - "router-instances/9494-47bd9338be61/router.log - the --ca-web-address launch."
  - "%TEMP%\\muse-router-probe-20260921\\{wsl,win}-capture.log - the two control probes."
